{
  "key": "pr-708",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(sm): honor mutexExcludeSelf in the action-time mutex re-check (🚨 #703 follow-up)",
    "description": "## 🚨 Regression fix (unresolved BLOCKING thread on merged #703)

The action-time mutex re-check (#703) ran for EVERY validate_pr rule with query.mutex — including revalidate-armed/revalidate-armed-green whose candidates SELF-HOLD ai_validating with mutexExcludeSelf:true. Self-holding candidates got blocked by their own label → leaked holder stacks could no longer drain (fa#1068/#577 family).

## Fix
validationMutexHeldByAnother now tracks selfHolds during the live scan and returns 0 when query.mutexExcludeSelf && selfHolds — mirroring githubSource's blocked = !selfHolds && otherHolds contract. Non-excludeSelf queries keep full any-other-holder blocking (the #703 double-arm protection intact). Probe moved after the cheap guards (carried 💡).

## Tests
Repro confirmed red pre-fix via stash (261/1), green post-fix; self-only-holder + stripped-arm mirrors. smAgent 262/0 · mergeBot 27/0 · smJiraSource 3/0."
  }
}

