{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: extract the duplicated probe-and-refuse block**

The pattern `var holder = validationMutexHeldByAnother(...); if (holder) { log; continue; }` now appears twice in `processRule` (latch-skip arm site, dispatch arm site), with only the variable name differing. A small helper would keep the two call sites in lockstep if the refusal semantics ever change again:

```javascript
function refuseArmIfMutexHeld(effectiveRepoInfo, rule, ticket, key) {
    var holder = validationMutexHeldByAnother(effectiveRepoInfo, rule, ticket);
    if (holder) {
        console.log('  🔒 ' + key + ' arm refused — pr-' + holder +
                    ' already holds ai_validating (action-time re-check;' +
                    ' the query-time mutex scanned a stale list)');
        return true; // NOT processedKeys — the slot stays with the holder
    }
    return false;
}
```

GraalJS-compatible (`var`, plain function). Non-blocking — the current duplication is tolerable and matches the file's explicit-comment style.
